{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And whoever remains</b> — who is poor and whose hand does not reach money to go up." "<b>Let them lift him</b> — let them give him loads and gifts. Or, 'let them lift him' — let them raise him, from the matter of 'high and lifted up' [רם ונשא], for the poor man is low, and this is the correct interpretation." "<b>With the freewill offering</b> — that they shall lift him along with the other freewill offerings that they donate."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:34.338419742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}